[size=4][b]Camp Everywhere[/b][/size]
[i]Smart Resting[/i]

Make camp wherever it makes sense, not only at the fixed camp spots. Put your Camp Supplies on a quick slot, look for a good place, and set up camp right there.

[size=3][b]How it works[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Put [b]Camp Supplies[/b] on any of the four quick slots.
[*]Press that quick slot. A ghost of the camp fire ring appears in front of you and follows you around: [color=#80ffb3][b]green[/b][/color] where you can camp, [color=#ff7060][b]red[/b][/color] where you can't.
[*]Press the quick slot again. On green, the camp is set up. On red, the ghost disappears.
[*]Walk up to your camp and use it like any other camp spot.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Where you can camp[/b][/size]

The ghost turns red when the spot is:
[list]
[*]under a roof (tree tops don't count)
[*]in a town or village (people or buildings all around)
[*]too steep or much higher or lower than where you stand
[*]in water, or you are swimming
[*]close to enemies (uses the game's own check)
[/list]

[size=3][b]Good to know[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Making camp is the game's own logic: same prompt, same Survival skill requirement, one Camp Supplies per camp, same camp menu.
[*]Placing the ghost or the camp uses up nothing. Camp Supplies are only used when you actually make camp.
[*]You have one camp at a time. Setting up a new one removes the old one.
[*]Camps are not saved. After loading a save, your camp is gone, so your save files stay clean.
[*]Camp Supplies you buy or pick up later can go on a quick slot automatically.
[*]Works with keyboard and controller, since it simply uses the game's quick slots.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS/releases/tag/experimental-latest]UE4SS[/url] (experimental build; tested with v3.0.1-1181)
[/list]

[size=3][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install UE4SS: put [code]dwmapi.dll[/code] and the [code]ue4ss[/code] folder into [code]ofAshAndSteel\ofAshAndSteelGame\Binaries\Win64\[/code].
[*]Extract this mod into your game folder [code]ofAshAndSteel\[/code]. The mod ends up in [code]ofAshAndSteelGame\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods\CampEverywhere\[/code].
[*]Start the game. The file [code]enabled.txt[/code] in the mod folder turns the mod on.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Steam Deck / Linux (Proton)[/b][/size]

Add this to the game's launch options in Steam so UE4SS gets loaded:
[code]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="dwmapi=n,b" %command%[/code]
Keep any launch options you already use after [code]%command%[/code].

[size=3][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]

Delete [code]ue4ss\Mods\CampEverywhere\[/code]. The mod doesn't change any game files or save data.

[size=3][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Tested on Steam build 24202860 (October 2026), Steam Deck with Proton 11.
[*]Works alongside .pak mods such as Immersive Road Signs and Choose What You Are Selling.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Towns and villages are recognized by the people and buildings around you. A lonely hut or a group of travellers in the wild can turn the ghost red.
[*]The ghost shows the fire ring only. That is also what a camp spot looks like before you use it.
[/list]
